<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31240" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nŏtĭus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νότιος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>southern</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">notia sidera,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Manil. 1, 436</span></i>
			; so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">piscis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 1, 427</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">polus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hyg. Astron. 1, 5</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">4, 11</span></i>.
			According to Pliny, <i>the Tyrrhene Sea</i> was called
			by some Greek writers Mare Notium, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 5,
				10, § 75</span></i>.</div>
